REM plan-122-F: term::setBackground takes ONE color::Color, not three Bytes.
REM
REM Each line is a distinct rejection class for the new signature. The old fixture
REM passed three channels; mechanically wrapping those in color::rgb(...) would have
REM moved the type error inside color::rgb and stopped testing term::setBackground
REM at all, so the cases are restated against the signature that now exists.

IMPORT term
IMPORT color

FUNC main AS Integer
  REM No arguments at all.
  term::setBackground()
  REM The pre-plan-122-F three-channel form: now an arity error, and the diagnostic
  REM should name term.setBackground rather than silently accepting it.
  term::setBackground(1, 2, 3)
  REM One argument, but not a colour.
  term::setBackground(255)
  REM Too many, even with a correct first argument.
  term::setBackground(color::rgb(1, 2, 3), 4)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
